      <Desc>ORGANIZED GROUPS TO RESUCE ANIMALS THROUGHOUT CALIFORNIA LOCATING RESCUES THAT HAVE BEEN NEGLECTED AND ABANDONED. EDUCATING PUBLIC OF THE PLIGHT OF HOMELESS ANIMALS VIA FACEBOOK AND OTHER SOCIAL MEDIAS ENCOURAGING ADOPTION. SUCCESS IN LOCATING AND PLACING ANIMALS IN FOREVER HOMES</Desc>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>0</ExpenseAmt>
        <GrantAmt>0</GrantAmt>
        <RevenueAmt>0</RevenueAmt>
        <Desc>In August 2024, we got a heartbreaking call from a rescuer in Mexico about a backyard breeding operation that had spiraled completely out of control. A man was breeding and selling dogs purely for profit, with no concern for their well-being. What rescuers found was devastating: exhausted mama dogs who had been bred over and over, some barely out of puppyhood themselves and more than 30 dogs in total who were desperate for help. They were living in filthy, overcrowded kennels. Many were malnourished, some suffering from untreated genetic conditions, and all were terrified. We knew we couldnt turn our backs. So, we said yes. Yes to all 30+ dogs, and immediately began the long road to healing. aking in that many dogs at once was overwhelming both emotionally and financially. We spent over $20,000 on vet care, treatments, and the slow, patient work of helping each dog learn to trust again. Every single one had their own story of survival and one by one, they started to bloom. Today, every one of those dogs has found a forever home across Southern California. Seeing their photos... running free, curled up on soft beds, loved beyond measure... brings tears to our eyes every time.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
